\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Holds Steady Vs Yen As Japan MOF Supports  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 870 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2004\par 06:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar held steady against the yen in Asia Wednesday, with its overnight slide on disappointing U.S. consumer confidence data grinding to a halt thanks to Japanese authorities' efforts to prop up the greenback.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the dollar above Y108.07 overnight, was reported to have been in the market again in Tokyo time - most likely to keep the dollar from completely erasing the gains it logged during last week's rally, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "When you look at how far the dollar slid against almost all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  except the yen last night - the obvious question is, who else (but Japan's MOF) would be buying the dollar? No one," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 "Like last night, today's price moves are also highly unnatural," he said, noting that the dollar was immediately bid higher the second it touched Y108.07 - the day's low.  \par \par \uc2 But it wasn't as if traders were caught off guard, as Japanese officials continued to give fair warning to the market.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bureaucrat Wednesday reminded markets the MOF continues to keep a close eye on the yen. Market movements "look natural, but in any case, we are watching market movements closely," said Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs.  \par \par \uc2 Market players also refrained from actively chasing the greenback lower against the euro, as they remained torn over whether it was safe to declare the dollar's rebound as being over, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 "While sentiment remains mixed, the euro is likely to move in a broad range of $1.25 to $1.30, although the closer it gets to $1.30, the greater the likelihood of a backlash from eurozone officials," said Katsuhiro Kaneko, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Mitsubishi Securities.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y108.17, little changed from Y108.15 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y108.68 late Tuesday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2678, lower than $1.2685 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2531 in Tokyo Tuesday. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y137.14, down from Y137.20 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y136.22 in Tokyo late Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8894, down from $1.8910 in New York but higher than $1.8627 in Tokyo Tuesday. [ 25-02-04 0547GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 While \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the dollar is unpopular with many market players, Tokyo received unexpected but qualified support for its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy from the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 IMF Managing Director Horst Koehler said Wednesday he believes Japan's massive yen-selling campaign is a "pragmatic" way to fight deflation given a lack of other monetary policy options.  \par \par \uc2 "I do think it was an appropriate policy stance," Koehler told a press conference after wrapping up two days of talks with Japanese officials here, including Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi, Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki and Economy and Banking Minister Heizo Takenaka.  \par \par \uc2 Koehler added, however, that he believes Japanese officials see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as "a temporary policy," and are not trying to bolster exporters by fixing the yen's exchange rate at an unfairly low level.  \par \par \uc2 The head of the IMF also toed the international community's line on the Chinese yuan, saying that it's in Beijing's interest to have a flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system, but that it's also important to respect China's wish for a gradual shift in the yuan regime.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were little moved by Wednesday's start to six-way talks aimed at ending North Korea's nuclear program. The talks are being held in Beijing between China, North and South Korea, Japan, the U.S. and Russia.  \par \par \uc2 The only way the yen would get a substantial boost from these talks is if there is great progress - a highly unlikely scenario, said J.P. Morgan Chase Bank strategist Tohru Sasaki.  \par \par \uc2 Sasaki added that even in the event some progress is made in the talks, the market's initial reaction may wind up being mixed, given that a good outcome - which would ease geopolitical risks for the U.S. as well as Japan, would be positive for both the yen and the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Instead of the six-way talks, market players are now focusing their attention on U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's testimony on the economy, which will be held before the House Budget Committee, to be held later in the global session, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX [ 25-02-04 0631GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040225e02p0005z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
