\par\par \b \uc2 Osaka Shares End Lower In Wake Of 5-Session US Stock Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2004\par 08:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--Shares traded on the Osaka Securities Exchange fell Wednesday in the wake of the five-session drop in U.S. stocks and on the view that the recent rise of the dollar against the yen may end soon.  \par \par \uc2 The Osaka market's adjusted average ended down 0.6% at 17943.23. Decliners outnumbered gainers 63 to 26, while 10 issues remained flat.  \par \par \uc2 In New York Tuesday, the Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 0.4% and the Nasdaq slipped 0.1%.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar stayed in the Y108s in Tokyo trading hours, and traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. But the general reaction among equity market participants was cool as many players regard the recent strength of the dollar as a short-term phenomenon.  \par \par \uc2 In Osaka, Namura Shipbuilding ended down 7.4% at Y464 after yesterday cutting its group net earnings outlook for this fiscal year to a Y1.8 billion loss from its prior estimate for a Y360 million profit.  \par \par \uc2 Other decliners included electronic components maker Murata Manufacturing, down 0.3% at Y5,880; custom-made LSI maker Rohm, down 2.3% at Y12,410; and Nintendo, down 2.1% at Y10,160.  \par \par \uc2 Retail investors snapped up Uehara Sei Shoji, a wholesaler and retailer of petroleum and other energy products. The issue ended up 17% at Y465, topping Y400 for the first time since September 1999 on the view that the financially healthy firm could make a good candidate for takeover bids, an Iwai Securities researcher.  \par \par \uc2 Fertilizer and industrial chemicals maker Taki Chemical also rose on bargain-hunting, ending up 3.6% at Y290 after saying its group net profit for the fiscal year ended December rose 10% to Y725 million, beating its initial target for Y580 million.  \par \par \uc2 Players worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market gyrations turned to domestic-demand issues such as Santen Pharmaceutical, which ended up 4.9% at Y1,493 after nosing into the Y1,500s for the first time since May 2002. [ 25-02-04 0721GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020040225e02p0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
