\par\par \b \uc2 Treasurys Stuck In Range In Quiet Tokyo Trade;Focus On  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 419 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2004\par 07:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--U.S. Treasurys were little moved in quiet Tokyo trade Tuesday ahead of key U.S. employment data due next week, although recent yen strength and the resulting expectation of less Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to weigh on the U.S. bonds.  \par \par \uc2 Around 0530 GMT, the 10-year note was up 3/32 at 99 22/32 to yield 4.04%. The 30-year issue was last trading up 4/32 at 106 31/32 to yield 4.91%.  \par \par \uc2 Treasury yields remain stuck in a recent range as the market lacks incentives to drive trade.  \par \par \uc2 Adjustments in the yen's strength, however, have started to weigh on the market, "because for the past half year or so, (Treasury) tenders were supported by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  money," said a senior trader at a securities house. The expectations for less aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts by Japanese authorities may send the 10-year Treasury yield to 4.3-4.5% from the current 4% level, the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 But the impact of less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be gradual, as "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be selling what they've already bought," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The main upcoming economic indicator is the U.S. jobs report due next week. Until then, Treasury market players will focus on comments by Federal Reserve officials.  \par \par \uc2 "Some market people are saying that a rate hike is possible later this year," but the chances are still only slim, the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Prices at 0530 GMT: \par    COUPON  MATURITY    PRICE   CHANGE    YIELD   CHANGE \par    1 7/8%   2-year  100 13/32  Unchanged  1.65%  -1.0 BPS \par    2 1/4%   3-year  101  7/32  Up  1/32   2.18%  -1.0 BPS \par    3%       5-year   99 31/32  Up  1/32   3.00%  -2.0 BPS \par    4%      10-year   99 22/32  Up  3/32   4.04%  -1.0 BPS \par    5 3/8%  30-year  106 31/32  Up  4/32   4.91%  -1.0 BPS \par    2-10-Yr Yield Spread: 234 BPS Vs 234 BPS \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the Chicago Board of Trade, the March bond futures contract was at 113 1/32, up 6/32 from the previous session. The most-heavily traded December Eurodollar contract on the Singapore Exchange was at 98.23, up from 98.22 Monday at the Chicago close.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Asako Tanabe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; asako.tanabe@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by John Gibson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1079 4041  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040224e02o00076\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
