\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Edges Higher But New Incentives Sought  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2004\par 06:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar edged higher against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia Tuesday, but trading was sluggish as investors held out for fresh incentives.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback has held to relatively narrow ranges since it rebounded sharply against the yen, euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. But traders said enough unwanted bets against the dollar remain in the market that any dollar-positive news could spark renewed short covering and push it sharply higher.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is struggling with (dollar-short) positions that risk losing money, but they can't find a good reason to buy dollars," said the head dealer at a European brokerage in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 Many investors were hoping upcoming Congressional testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan would provide the dollar with new direction - perhaps in the form of clues on the timing of a possible U.S. rate hike.  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan is slated to testify before the Senate Banking Committee later Tuesday and the House Budget Committee on the economy Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's finance minister welcomed the recent rebound in the dollar, saying it was a correction of speculative movements.  \par \par \uc2 "It appears that such movements are being reassessed," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ordered yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the dollar above Y108.00 after its recent upswing - although the MOF's covert dollar bids are harder to spot when the greenback is rallying and many players are looking to buy.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very difficult to distinguish who's bidding, but it's quite possible that they've been in the market to support the dollar," the brokerage dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y108.68, above Y108.33 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y108.73 late Monday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2531, lower than $1.2552 late Monday in New York. The euro was at $1.2505 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y136.22, up from Y136.01 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y136.01 in Tokyo late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8627, down from $1.8664 in New York but higher than $1.8572 in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Following the ministry's standard practice, Tanigaki's deputy, Vice Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, declined to comment on whether the MOF had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 He said only that there was no change to the ministry's standing policy of acting against excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings.  \par \par \uc2 That didn't stop traders and analysts from speculating about changes in the ministry's stance.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF appears to have drawn a new "line in the sand" for the dollar around Y108.00, above the Y105.00 level it had apparently defended since the start of the year, BNP Paribas said in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 The brokerage said the ministry may be tempted to keep nudging the dollar higher ahead of Japan's fiscal year-end in March, when most Japanese exporters close their books.  \par \par \uc2 Those same exporters, however, may cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise close to Y109.00, as the dollar's climb above that level for the first time since late last year gives them "extra incentive to increase sales," it said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's downside, meanwhile, could be supported by the reduction of investment-related hedges thanks to an improved outlook for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The size of the dollar's recent rebound has surprised Japanese investors, many of whom had hedged \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk on their U.S. holdings on the assumption that the dollar wouldn't trade much above Y105.00 before the March fiscal-year end, a Tokyo dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "Now they're starting to think a Y107-Y112 range could hold," he said. "Many of them would like to buy dollars back."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040224e02o0005y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
