\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar fights back after recent drubbing.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2004\par 13:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 20 (Reuters) - The dollar powered to six-week highs against the yen and hit two-week peaks versus the euro on Friday as investors bought back the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after months of dumping it across the board.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts viewed this as a temporary pause in the dollar's two-year downtrend but said the euro's sharp pullback from Wednesday's record highs above $1.29 meant new peaks for Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term looked less likely.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is taking a breather before its next assault on $1.30 and we are seeing an unwinding of short dollar positions," said Mark McFarland, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said technical trade was dominating, though U.S. consumer price data at 1330 GMT and speeches from several Federal Reserve officials would be eyed for clues on the future path of U.S. interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is nervous after the roller coaster ride we've seen and speculators are driving the action," said Michael Klawitter, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at West LB.  \par \par \uc2 By 1242 GMT, the dollar was three quarters of a percent higher against the yen at 107.85 and half a percent higher against the euro at $1.2655.  \par \par \uc2 High-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have outperformed this month, also succumbed to the greenback's rebound. Sterling was nursing losses of 0.8 percent at $1.8784 while the Australian dollar was down three quarters of a percent at US$0.7855.  \par \par \uc2 BUYING IT BACK  \par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer inflation figures are expected to show a 0.1 percent rise in the core reading and a 0.3 percent rise in the headline figure for January.  \par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of St Louis President William Poole is due to speak on the state of the U.S. economy at 1345 GMT and Fed board governor Ben Bernanke is slated to make a speech at 1745 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan is due to speak on education in the economy at 1845 GMT. No question and answer session is expected.  \par \par \uc2 The fact that short term players such as momentum and hedge funds were driving much of the dollar's rebound bolstered the perception this did not yet amount to a turning point for the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing a broad correction now, which is mainly technical," said Trevor Dinmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The price action above $1.29 was disappointing and convinced some players that we may not see an immediate move to $1.30."  \par \par \uc2 This week, fresh comments from European officials fuelled nervousness that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling euros, particularly if the euro extends its rally into the $1.30-$1.35 zone.  \par \par \uc2 Yen traders were also keen to unwind short dollar positions since persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been successful in keeping the greenback above the psychologically important 105 yen level.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040220e02k001lv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
