\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Higher Vs Yen On Speculative Buybacks  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 854 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2004\par 07:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar advanced against the yen in Asia Friday as short-term players bought back the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after support for the unit proved solid.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback also got a lift against the euro from profit-taking by speculators in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Although few analysts believe the dollar's two-year-slide against its major rivals is over, its short-term outlook has brightened after it escaped recent major events generally unscathed.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar failed to break below key points even after major events like the Group of Seven meeting and Japan's gross domestic product data," said Tatsuro Karitani, vice president of Mizuho Corporate Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division. "It makes sense for players to feel like taking profits (on other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) now."  \par \par \uc2 The market considers Y105 a key level for the dollar, and $1.30 a significant barrier for the euro, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Some Tokyo traders said U.S. hedge funds had accumulated "substantial dollar-short positions" against the yen ahead of the G7 summit earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit held above the key Y105 mark despite a failure by G7 leaders to call for a stronger dollar, unwillingness by U.S. central bankers' to raise interest rates, and breathtaking growth in Japanese economy's between October and December. Resilience in the face of these factors has prompted fund managers to buy back dollars, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Players waited a long time, "but prices didn't change - it's gameover," said Katsunori Kitakura, senior manager at the Chuo Mitsui Trust and Banking Co's treasury department.  \par \par \uc2 Traders also attributed the dollar's rise to persistent yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry defending Y105.  \par \par \uc2 The buying of dollars for yen by U.S. hedge funds was a major force that pushed the pair close to 107.50 in late Asian trade Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro hit an intraday high of $1.2765 early, but soon lost ground as speculators unwound positions.  \par \par \uc2 At 0520 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y107.45, above Y107.04 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y106.71 late Thursday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2705, lower than $1.2713 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $1.2707 in Tokyo Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y136.55, up from Y136.10 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y135.28 in Tokyo late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8932, down from $1.8944 in New York but higher than $1.8865 in Tokyo Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 But the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rise against the yen and the euro may just be temporary position adjustments, some strategists said.  \par \par \uc2 "It's too early to declare the end of the dollar bearish trend," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas' in Tokyo. Low U.S. interest rates, a suspected U.S. preference for a weak dollar, and widening U.S. budget and current account deficits are expected to drag the greenback lower in weeks ahead, she said. The U.S. twin deficits, left to expand, may eventually spark a rise in long-term interest rates, which would hurt the U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 Fink added that the yen may gain on speculation Japanese stocks and bonds will attract more overseas investors given the recently announced annualized gross domestic product growth of 7% in the three months ended Dec. 31.  \par \par \uc2 Non-Japanese investors have been net buyers of Japanese shares for 10 straight months since April 2003, and net buyers of Japanese bonds between last November and January, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data.  \par \par \uc2 "The Nikkei 225 Stock Average index is showing signs of recovering, and if overseas capital continues to flow into Japan, there'll be upward pressure on the yen," said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 Traders also speculated European authorities wouldn't take any action in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, or cut interest rates. Some traders expect the euro to move into the low $1.30s and hit $1.35 by early March.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't believe the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Fink said. Its goal to make the euro a second base \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar requires letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  float according to market forces and raising investor confidence in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said.  \par \par \uc2 "But if the euro surges to $1.35 too fast, (Europeans) may begin to seriously fret," and consider \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an option, Fink said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale and Bennett Richardson  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040220e02k0006e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
