\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar falls - little impact from jobless claims.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2004\par 16:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds comment, changes dateline; previous LONDON)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped against some major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday on a mild bout of profit-taking from gains posted after weekly U.S. jobless claims fell more sharply than expected, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar spiked briefly after the government said new claims for state unemployment benefits dropped to 344,000 in the week ended Feb. 14 from a revised 368,000 the previous week. The market had expected 353,000 new claims.  \par \par \uc2 But the closely watched four-week moving average, seen as a more reliable measure of the pace of U.S. layoffs, rose slightly, to 352,000 from 351,750.  \par \par \uc2 However, the dollar's gains proved to be short-lived.  \par \par \uc2 "You would have to expect some consolidation after the big move yesterday. The euro has gone to $1.2900 a couple of times now. Today will be a day of consolidation where the dollar finds a range here," said Grant Wilson, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with Mellon Bank, in Pittsburgh.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In morning New York trade, the euro was trading higher against the\par dollar at $1.2690 . The dollar rose 0.1 percent against the yen to\par 107.00 yen  and was trading slightly lower against the Swiss franc at\par 1.2426 francs       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sterling, recently pushed higher on expectations of a rate hike, traded at $1.8922 , up about 0.3 percent.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UK retail sales rose at the fastest annual pace in more than a year in January, raising the likelihood of more Bank of England interest rate rises and further enhancing prospects for sterling.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I think on balance, the (jobless claims) report is consistent with continued, moderate but sluggish improvement in the labor market. The upside surprise may help the dollar sustain its gains from yesterday," said Alex Beuzelin, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market analyst at Ruesch International in Washington.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But he doubted whether the data would have a positive long-term impact on the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "Bigger picture, this is the type of data that will make the Fed remain on hold for a while. This should be a negative for the dollar," Beuzelin said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Low U.S. interest rates of 1 percent are one of the reasons cited by analysts for the dollar's two-year slide, with the diminished appeal of U.S. assets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MORE U.S. DATA, EUROPE WARINESS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the data front, the Philadelphia Federal Reserve Bank was to release its February manufacturing conditions index at noon EST (1700 GMT). Forecasts are for a decline to 35.0 versus 38.8 in January.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Several Federal Reserve officials are also scheduled to speak.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets were on the lookout for comments from Europe about potential damage to the fragile European economy from a strong euro.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In recent sessions, such comments fueled nervousness that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap the euro as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  targets $1.30, although analysts believe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely before that level.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar staged a strong recovery against the euro, yen and Swiss franc on Wednesday, partly helped by warnings from European politicians about the euro's strength.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in early Asian trade on Thursday also served to support the trend, although at the European open, the greenback was below the highs set by the New York close.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by John Parry in New York and Justyna Pawlak in London).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040219e02j002bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
