\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro struggles to recover recent losses vs dollar.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Justyna Pawlak  \par \uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2004\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The euro strained to recoup the previous day's losses against the dollar on Thursday after a two cent fall from a record peak and the market was trying to gauge if the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's long rally was due a bigger pause.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar staged a strong recovery on the euro, yen and Swiss franc on Wednesday, partly helped by warnings from European politicians about the euro's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early Asian trade on Thursday also served to support the trend although at the European open the greenback was below the highs set by the New York close.  \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing large intra-day ranges for the G3 (U.S., euro zone and Japan) \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and this will continue for a while," said Bilal Hafeez, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in London.  \par \par \uc2 "Basically, there is a conflict in the market with investors being very short dollars, on one hand, and policy makers introducing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  uncertainty, on the other."  \par \par \uc2 By 1240 GMT the euro had recovered a third of a percent from its closing levels to $1.2715 but was still two cents below a record high of $1.2927 set early on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar held steady on the day at 106.77 yen having rallied by more than one yen on Wednesday from near three-year lows.  \par \par \uc2 Some said they thought the dollar reversal had begun in dollar/yen, possibly with the help of well-disguised Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and then spread to other dollar pairs.  \par \par \uc2 Britain's sterling was getting a lot of attention on Thursday after strong retail sales numbers helped it rise to a one-year high against the euro around 67.00 pence.  \par \par \uc2 PIECES OF THE PUZZLE  \par \par \uc2 Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could get fresh momentum from a series of U.S. data, scheduled for release later in the session.  \par \par \uc2 Weekly U.S. jobless claims are due at 1330 GMT, with forecasts for 353,000 new filings compared with 363,000 in the prior week.  \par \par \uc2 The Philadelphia Federal Reserve Bank releases its February manufacturing conditions index at 1700. Forecasts are for a decline to 35.0 versus 38.8 in January.  \par \par \uc2 Several Federal Reserve officials are also scheduled to speak.  \par \par \uc2 But markets were also on the lookout for comments from Europe about potential damage to the fragile European economy from a strong euro.  \par \par \uc2 In recent sessions, such comments fuelled nervousness that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the euro as it set its sights on $1.30, although analysts still believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely before that level.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, French President Jacques Chirac said the euro zone seemed to be bearing the brunt of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility and German Economy Minister Wolfgang Clement said he had a level in mind at which the ECB should halt the euro's rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 However deputy Belgian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Luc Coene said on Thursday it was naive to think unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB could change the tide and that it was "out of the question" that the United States would be willing to join in.  \par \par \uc2 The ECB holds a governing council meeting on Thursday but is not expected to discuss monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMIC DATA  \par \par \uc2 German data showed the economy grew an anaemic 0.2 percent in the fourth quarter of last year as consumer spending remained sluggish and the strong euro held back exports.  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone trade numbers showed the bloc's surplus at a higher-than-expected 5.7 billion euros in December.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, UK retail sales rose at the fastest annual pace in more than a year in January, raising the likelihood of more Bank of England interest rate rises to cool demand.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling, recently under upward pressure from rate hike prospects, traded at $1.8964, up more than half a percent on the day but still below Wednesday's 11-year high of $1.9140.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling also hit a 14-month peak against its trade-weighted index at 105.8.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040219e02j00220\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
