\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro stages hesitant bounce after drubbing.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Charlotte Cooper  \par \uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2004\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The euro attempted a small rebound on the dollar on Thursday after the previous day's two cent fall from a record peak but the market was trying to gauge if the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally was due a bigger pause.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar staged a strong recovery on the euro, yen and Swiss franc on Wednesday, partly helped by warnings from European politicians about the euro's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early Asian trade on Thursday also served to support the reversal although by the European open the greenback was below the highs it had set by the New York close.  \par \par \uc2 "Everyone was taken by surprise by the sharp correction of the dollar and snowballing closing of short dollar positions," said Niels Christensen, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is still shell-shocked and it needs to find its feet."  \par \par \uc2 By 0845 GMT the euro had recovered a third of a percent from its closing levels to $1.2715 but was still two cents below a record high of $1.2927 set early on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was a shade lower on the day at 106.70 yen having rallied by more than one yen on Wednesday from near three-year lows. Some said they thought the dollar reversal had begun in dollar/yen, possibly with the help of well-disguised Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and then spread to other dollar pairs.  \par \par \uc2 EURO TALK  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, French President Jacques Chirac said the euro zone seemed to be bearing the brunt of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility and German Economy Minister Wolfgang Clement said he had a level in mind at which the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should halt the euro's rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said these remarks fuelled the euro/dollar reversal from its highs, with the market nervous of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the closer the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  got to $1.30.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar got a further boost from euro officials' remarks suggesting a need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it's too early to say the dollar is on a genuine recovery path as there are no prospects of higher interest rates yet," said Tomoko Fujii, market and economic analysis director at Nikko Citigroup in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 However deputy Belgian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Luc Coene said on Thursday it was naive to think unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB could change the tide but that it was "out of the question" that the United States would be willing to join in.  \par \par \uc2 The ECB holds a governing council meeting on Thursday but is not expected to discuss monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 German data showed the economy grew an anaemic 0.2 percent in the fourth quarter of last year as consumer spending remained sluggish and the strong euro held back exports.  \par \par \uc2 US CALENDAR  \par \par \uc2 Weekly U.S. jobless claims are due at 1330 GMT, with forecasts for 353,000 new filings compared with 363,000 in the prior week.  \par \par \uc2 The Philadelphia Federal Reserve Bank releases its February business activity index at 1700. Forecasts are for a decline to 35.0 versus 38.8 in January.  \par \par \uc2 Several Federal Reserve officials are also scheduled to speak.  \par \par \uc2 The pound drifted 2-1/2 cents below the previous day's 11-year highs around $1.9140, while the Australian dollar was about a cent below seven-year highs around $0.80.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040219e02j001hf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
