\par\par \b \uc2 Fukuda:  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Not Manipulation To Aid Exports  \b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2004\par 03:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top government spokesman said Wednesday he doesn't want to give the impression that yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is aimed at assisting the nation's export industry.  \par \par \uc2 "There's also \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability. I wouldn't want it to be thought that we are manipulating the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the sake of exports," Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda said.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF's official stance on the yen is that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should reflect economic fundamentals and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to combat sudden swings caused by speculative trading.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have spent staggering amounts to slow the dollar's fall in recent months. They sold Y7 trillion in January alone and market players say the government likely spent several trillion more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month in an effort to stop the dollar dropping below Y105.  \par \par \uc2 Surging exports have played a significant role in helping Japan's gross domestic product grow over the last year. Earlier Wednesday, government figures showed October-December GDP was up 1.7% from the previous quarter, the fastest pace of expansion in 13 years and the fourth straight quarter of growth.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040218e02i00022\par }