\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Dlr/Yen Vols Languish; Euro Vols Stay Bid  \b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2004\par 21:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by one-month dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options in New York Tuesday remain stuck at three-year lows due to a moribund spot market, but euro/dollar options are well bid as the euro once again threatens to test its record high.  \par \par \uc2 On the one hand, dollar/yen options are really cheap at these levels, which should boost demand. But the spot exchange rate has been stuck in an extremely tight range following the Group of Seven's meeting in Boca Raton, Fla., earlier February. This means there is virtually no opportunity to trade the option at a profit.  \par \par \uc2 "You just can't make any money being long of vols, even within the (spot) range," said an options dealer in New York.  \par \par \uc2 After G7 finance chiefs warned that "excess volatility and disorderly movements in exchange rates are undesirable," dealers are convinced that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a green light to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market selling yen in order to keep the dollar above Y105.00. There is speculation that the ministry will defend this level through March 31, the end of Japan's fiscal year, according to dealers.  \par \par \uc2 That only leaves dollar/yen with room to move on the upside, although heavy offers from Japanese exporters and good foreign demand for Japanese assets continue to put upward pressure on the yen. Not even the dollar's brief spike up to Y106.00 earlier Tuesday could lift vols.  \par \par \uc2 In contrast, the dollar's moves against the major European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday have been much sharper, which is keeping volatilities well bid. The euro, which flirted with its all-time high of $1.2898 Friday before sliding sharply, finds itself back above $1.28 Tuesday and looking to launch another assault on that high, while sterling smashed its way up through $1.90 to print another 11-year high.  \par \par \uc2 Options-related selling in the euro, however, is providing stiff resistance, with a large Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said to be defending a double-no-touch option with the upside at $1.2900 and support around $1.2650.  \par \par \uc2 "And the closer we get to $1.30 people become a little bit skeptical of going too long of the spot so they decide to go through the options," the options dealer said. This is providing options with a good bid Tuesday, he noted.  \par \par \uc2 Around 3 p.m. EST Tuesday in the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money euro/dollar options implied volatility of 11.10%/11.40%, compared with 10.90%/11.40% in Tokyo earlier Tuesday and 11.05%/11.40% in Tokyo Monday, when markets in the U.S. were closed for a national holiday.  \par \par \uc2 One-month quarter delta risk-reversals favored euro call/dollar put options by 0.3%/0.6%, up from 0.1%/0.4% toward the end of last week.  \par \par \uc2 One-month ATM dollar/yen options implied volatility of 7.40%/7.70%, compared with 7.40%/7.60% in Tokyo earlier Tuesday and 7.50%/7.90% in Tokyo Monday. That level from earlier Tuesday was the lowest one-month vols have traded since November 2000.  \par \par \uc2 One-month quarter delta risk-reversals favored yen call/dollar put options by 0.4%/0.8%, little changed from 0.5%/0.8%.  \par \par \uc2 One-month ATM euro/yen options were trading at 10.00%/10.30%, compared with around 10.50% in Tokyo Tuesday and 10.05%/10.35% in Tokyo Monday.  \par \par \uc2 At 3 p.m. EST, the dollar was at Y105.72, against Y105.68 in Tokyo Tuesday and Y105.42 late Monday in London. The euro was at $1.2840, up from $1.2767 and $1.2784, while against the yen it was up at Y135.68 from Y134.91 and Y134.75.  \par \par \uc2 -Jamie McGeever; Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2096; jamie.mcgeever@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 1077 4127 44427  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040217e02h000tv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
