\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar pushes up vs yen on BOJ jitters.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2004\par 08:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against the yen on Tuesday to its highest level in 11 days as traders grew nervous about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the spike could have been due to yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ, while others said it was likely due to options-related buying or the yen's fall against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The move was a suspicious one and could have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I am just not sure," said a trader at a major Japanese bank.   \par \par \uc2 Last month, Japan spent a record seven trillion yen ($66.38 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The greenback jumped a quarter of a yen to 106.02 yen its highest since February 6.   \par \par \uc2 By 0642 GMT, it was at 105.81/86 yen compared with 105.42/52 in late European trade. U.S. markets were closed on Monday for Presidents Day.   \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.2767/72 little changed on the day.   \par \par \uc2 Sterling jumped over one yen to a five-year high around 200.20 yen while the euro hit a high of 135.31 yen   \par \par \uc2 Although the dollar fell to 3-= year lows around 105.15 yen last week, traders were getting hesitant about retesting those troughs on the view that the Japanese authorities were determined to defend the 105 yen level.   \par \par \uc2 "The lower end of the ranges have been so difficult to break, and people are having to wonder what they would have to do if they built up short dollar positions here," said Hiroyuki Watanabe, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Shinsei Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki reiterated on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at curbing speculative movements in the market.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  GDP AWAITED   \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the BOJ may have stepped in on Tuesday to push up the dollar ahead of Japan's October-December gross domestic product data due on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "If the figure comes out strong, the authorities will lose their justification for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially after the G7 (Group of Seven) countries said \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reflect fundamentals," said a senior trader at a Japanese trust bank.   \par \par \uc2 "Thus they may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push up the dollar beforehand since they are out to protect 105 yen."   \par \par \uc2 The market's consensus is for GDP growth of around five percent on an annualised basis, which would be stronger than the U.S. growth rate of four percent in the same quarter.   \par \par \uc2 Off-and-on rumours since last week that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or some of the national central banks in the region might have been selling euros were a sign that the market was also sensitive about the possibility of European authorities stepping into the market, traders added.   \par \par \uc2 ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet, pressed continually by European parliamentarians on Monday, declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market or would do so to curb the euro's strength.   \par \par \uc2 For now, traders were awaiting U.S. industrial production data for January due at 1415 GMT and monthly portfolio flow data from the U.S. Treasury.   \par \par \uc2 Output growth was forecast at 0.8 percent month-on-month in a Reuters poll after a rise of 0.1 percent in December. ($1=105.45 yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040218e02h0014e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
