\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar spikes up vs yen but gains limited.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2004\par 07:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The dollar spiked to a one-week high against the yen on Tuesday amid nervousness over Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but gains were capped as investors kept their gloomy outlook on the greenback on concerns about the U.S. deficits.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped about a quarter of a yen to a high of 105.99 , but it soon met with selling and was pushed back to stand at 105.82/87 yen by 0525 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 Some traders said the greenback's jump could have been due to yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while others said it was likely due to options-related buying.   \par \par \uc2 "The move was a suspicious one and could have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I am just not sure," said a trader at a major Japanese bank.   \par \par \uc2 Last month, Japan spent a record seven trillion yen ($66.38 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Although the dollar fell to 3-= year lows around 105.15 yen last week, traders were getting hesitant about retesting those troughs as the perception grew that the Japanese authorities were determined to defend the 105 yen level.   \par \par \uc2 "The lower end of the ranges have been so difficult to break, and people are having to wonder what they would have to do if they built up short dollar positions here," said Hiroyuki Watanabe, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Shinsei Bank.   \par \par \uc2 The euro was trading at $1.2767/72 , little changed on the day.   \par \par \uc2 On the macro-economic front, the market was keeping a close eye on how the Japanese stock market would react to Japan's October-December gross domestic product data due on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The market's consensus is for growth of around five percent on an annualised basis, which would be stronger than the U.S. growth rate of four percent in the same quarter. Traders said such a strong reading could undermine the Japanese government's case for continuing its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Although I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will end soon, this is the biggest threat for the dollar versus the yen," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Off-and-on rumours since last week that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or some of the national central banks in the region might have been selling euros were a sign that the market was also sensitive about the possibility of European authorities stepping into the market, traders added.   \par \par \uc2 ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet, pressed continually by European parliamentarians on Monday, declined to comment on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market or would do so to curb the euro's strength.   \par \par \uc2 For now, traders were awaiting U.S. industrial production data for January due at 1415 GMT and monthly portfolio flow data from the U.S. Treasury.   \par \par \uc2 Output growth was forecast at 0.8 percent month-on-month in a Reuters poll after a rise of 0.1 percent in December. ($1=105.45 yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040217e02h0016c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
