\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar stuck as BOJ jitters keep lid on yen.   \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2004\par 02:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 17 (Reuters) - The dollar shuffled in a tight range on Tuesday as investors refrained from testing a break below the key 105 yen level on expectations that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar would likely come under pressure from selling by Japanese investors repatriating U.S. Treasury coupon payments later in the day, but a steep fall was unlikely.   \par \par \uc2 "There shouldn't be any big moves because of this. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should absorb much of the selling," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 As of 0100 GMT, the dollar was flat at 105.47/52 yen.   \par \par \uc2 The euro was also little changed at $1.2768/73.   \par \par \uc2 Following thin trade on Monday due to a U.S. holiday, some players were looking ahead to Japan's fourth-quarter gross domestic product due on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The market's consensus is for growth of around five percent on an annualised basis, which would be stronger than the U.S. growth rate of four percent in the same quarter.   \par \par \uc2 "If it turns out that the Japanese economy is doing better, they (the government) would lose their justification for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sahara.   \par \par \uc2 "Although I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will end soon, this is the biggest threat for the dollar versus the yen."   \par \par \uc2 Ahead of the GDP figures, traders were awaiting U.S. industrial production data for January due at 1415 GMT and monthly portfolio flow data from the U.S. Treasury.   \par \par \uc2 Industrial production was forecast at 0.8 pct month-on-month in a Reuters poll. It came in at 0.1 pct in December.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet refused to be drawn on any suggestion by lawmakers that the ECB might consider interest rate changes to tackle euro strength, stressing that rates were at historically low levels and that they were appropriate.   \par \par \uc2 He also repeated that excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market volatility was undesirable.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040217e02h00148\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
