\par\par \b \uc2 EUROPEAN MORNING BRIEFING: US Holiday To Damp Trading  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2004\par 06:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US SUMMARY: Stocks Hit By Data, Treasurys Rise \par  \par DJIA         10627.85    loss 66.22    dn 0.6% \par NASDAQ        2053.56    loss 20.05    dn 0.97% \par S&P 500       1145.81    loss  6.30    dn 0.6% \par 10-Yr U.S. Treasury: 99 20/32 to yield 4.05% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Wall Street stock markets fell Friday on disappointing consumer sentiment data, while Treasurys rallied as investors covered bearish positions ahead of the holiday weekend. Markets wil be closed Monday for the Presidents Day holiday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 STOCKS: Early stock gains crumbled Friday after a surprise dip in consumer sentiment gave buyers a reason to step aside ahead of a three-day holiday weekend.  \par \par \uc2 Strong profits at Dell, the world's largest personal-computer maker, helped stocks rebound at the open. But gains reversed around 1000 EST on a report that the University of Michigan's mid-month reading on consumer sentiment dropped to 93.1 in February, from 103.8 in January. The number missed analysts' expectation of 104.  \par \par \uc2 Investors might have used the disappointing consumer-confidence report "as an excuse to take profits ahead of a long three-day weekend," said Michael Sheldon, chief market strategist at Spencer Clarke LLC. News that the U.S. trade gap widened in December also didn't help stocks to rise.  \par \par \uc2 Light trading volume ahead of the Presidents Day holiday Monday appeared to exaggerate the stock market's move lower.  \par \par \uc2 BONDS: Treasurys finished an event-packed week on a firm note, with data pointing to a souring of consumer sentiment, which kept all benchmarks in positive territory as market participants exited early ahead of the long weekend.  \par \par \uc2 A combination of short covering after soft data and earlier weakness in the U.S. dollar fueled the rise in Treasurys, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback reversed course and gained ground in late later in the day amid rumors of dollar buying by European monetary authorities. This helped curb some of the gains in the Treasury market.  \par \par \uc2 A weak dollar is viewed as bond market positive since it means the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets aggressively to weaken its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , will continue to recycle massive amounts dollars bought against the yen into U.S. government securities.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the Treasury gains, analysts agree that investors have some trepidation about investing in a market trading at the high end of what they view as an expensive trading range.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIAN SUMMARY: Stocks Edge Up, Domestic Demand Cos Lead \par USD-Yen:      105.47     gain 0.02      up 0.02% \par AUD-USD:      0.7899     gain 0.0001    up 0.03% \par Hang Seng:    13841.31   gain 101.85    up 0.7% \par Nikkei 225:   10568.57   gain 10.88     up 0.1% \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Tokyo stocks inched up Monday morning as investors bought stocks of companies that rely on domestic demand.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Technology and other exporter issues were mixed following Wall Street's weakness Friday, while domestic demand-related issues such as NTT and Tokyo Electric were among the gainers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trade was reported to be slow ahead of Monday's U.S. holiday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese government bonds were lower Monday due to small-lot selling and some profit-taking as stocks held firm. But trade was very thin before a 20-year bond tender Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pension funds and life insurers will likely be buyers of the new 20-year notes, as will curve players given the 20-year zone is relatively cheap compared to the 10-year sector, said Mask Mizzen, chief strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN OUTLOOK: Stocks, Bonds Seen Steady \par  \par Euro-USD      1.2725     loss 0.0005    dn 0.04% \par Stlg-USD      1.8822     loss 0.0025    dn 0.1%   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--European stocks are set for a lower open with corporate news in focus. Bonds are set for a steady start.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 STOCKS: European stocks are set to open slightly lower after Wall Street's fall Friday, but Monday's holiday in the U.S. and a lack of data will damp trade.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IG Index is calling the FTSE 100 down 6 points at 4406 and the DAX down 5 points at 4052.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks ended lower Friday, as disappointing economic data from the U.S. and a sagging healthcare sector damped enthusiasm for equities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vodafone will be in focus Monday after The Wall Street Journal reported it made a bid of about $35 billion for AT&T Wireless, roughly matching a bid made by Cingular Wireless. AT&T Wireless is believed to have asked both bidders to sweeten their offers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norsk Hydro, Sanofi-Synthelabo and Anglo American are among the companies reporting results Monday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BONDS: European government bonds should open steady, supported by gains in U.S. Treasurys Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's bond-supportive U.S. data will also continue to have an impact, but traders note that some investors appear nervous of entering the market at what they consider an over-priced level.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Some of our clients with neutral positions are unhappy about paying current prices to get back into the market," said one trader.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With U.S. investors away Monday for the President's Day holiday, liquidity is likely to be trimmed.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The dollar starts the session on a steady note Monday, posting gains against both the yen and euro.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Worries that the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to take some steam out of the euro's rally against the dollar kept the pair on a firm footing.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of Germany's Ifo institute was quoted in a Swiss daily Saturday saying that it was within the ECB's abilities to aim for a reduction in the euro/dollar rate through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders, however, said the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Europe is closer to rumor than fact at this stage.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Outside the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  threat, the risks for the dollar remain to the downside, traders say. A slew of data to be released out of the U.S. this week - including industrial production, housing starts and consumer prices for January - hold more risk than hope for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CALENDAR: Monday, Feb. 16: US Markets Closed \par GMT/EST Country Indicator/Event \par  \par 1400/0900  FRA  Weekly T-bill Auction results \par 1430/0930  GER  ECB calls for main refi bids \par N/A        US   All markets closed for Presidents Day \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Steve McGrath; Dow Jones Newswires; +42 (0)20-842-9284; steve.mcgrath@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Norsk Hydro (NHY): 4Q Earnings \par Consensus net income (Company, 20 analysts): NOK3.2B (NOK3.38B) \par Forecast range: NOK2.8B - NOK3.6B \par Note:  Low tax rate in 02 skews comparison, masks gains from high oil, gas prices and strong production growth, analysts say. "Expect upcoming 4Q results to offer little incremental to the investment story, other than a confirmation of current financial strength, high growth in E&P and highlight the continued weakness in the downstream aluminium market," Merrill Lynch says. \par  \par Sanofi-Synthelabo (SNY): FY Earnings \par Consensus net profit (DJ, 5 analysts): EUR2.02B (EUR1.76B) \par Consensus sales: EUR8.05B (N/A) \par Consensus EPS: EUR2.86 (EUR2.42) \par Note: Earnings seen overshadowed by its hostile bid for Aventis. Bryan Garnier analyst Roddolphe Besserve rates Sanofi at sell. Says if the deal goes through, the combined company will have a high risk profile and very poor growth prospects. \par  \par Anglo American Platinum (AMS.JO): expected to deliver FY 03 headline earnings of around ZAR9.55 a share, -64% from ZAR26.76 in 02. It gave guidance in Dec earnings will be down at least 30% due to the strong ZAR. "Mon's results shouldn't hold any surprises as the co's earnings and expansion plans were updated just 2-mos ago," says HSBC precious metals analyst Alan Cook. Stock -1.4% at ZAR300. (ANM) \par  \par  \par OTHER SCHEDULED EVENTS: \par  \par Merck KGaA (MRK.XE): FY Earnings press conference \par  \par Depfa Bank (DEP.XE): FY Earnings press conference \par  \par Stream Group (SEA.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par St Modwen Properties (SMP.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par EQ Group (EQI.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Itnet (ITN.LN): FY Earnings \par  \par Ipsos (7329.FR): FY Revenue \par  \par Pannonplast (PPLAST.BU): 4Q Earnings, New CEO to unveil restructuring plans \par  \par KGHM Polska Miedz (KGH.WA): 4Q Unconsolidated Earnings \par  \par Alfa Laval (ALFA.SK): 4Q Earnings \par  \par Skandia: FY Sales \par  \par Graphisoft (GRAPHI.BU): 4Q Earnings \par  \par Danubius (DANUBIUS.BU): 4Q Earnings \par  \par Agora (AGO.WA): 4Q Earnings \par  \par JM (JM.SK): 4Q Earnings \par  \par Hercules Property Services (HPS.LN): 1H Earnings \par  \par Austrian Air (AUA.VI): January traffic figures \par  \par Swiss Re (RUKN.VX): 2004 Renewals \par  \par Wireless Group (TWG.LN): EGM \par  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 1011  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040216e02g00064\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
