\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Steady Vs Majors Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2004\par 06:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar kept to tight ranges against the yen and euro Monday in Asia, as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe restrained dollar-bears.  \par \par \uc2 Many market participants were also sidelined with U.S. markets closed Monday for President's Day holiday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 In what has become almost a daily ritual, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were reported to have kept the dollar propped up against the yen by placing covert bids around Y105.30, traders said. That kept the dollar locked in an 18-sen band against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But in a newer development, Tokyo market players - spooked by the euro's sharp sell-off on Friday - also refrained from actively selling the dollar against the euro.  \par \par \uc2 While the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't believed to have had a hand in the dollar's sudden rebound against the euro on Friday, the pace and extent of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide shook the market nonetheless, making players extremely sensitive to rumors of any possible ECB action, or other euro-negative factors, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday in New York, the dollar reversed course on aggressive profit-taking to rally strongly against its major rivals after earlier sinking to new depths on weak U.S. economic data. Rumors that a major German bank had sold $2 billion worth of euros for dollars sparked speculation, though unconfirmed, of possible ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a trader at a major Japanese bank.  \par \par \uc2 "It's really hard to trade either the yen or the euro now given the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , be it physical or verbal," said Minoru Shioiri, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Mitsubishi Securities.  \par \par \uc2 Thus players are continuing to turn to high yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with firm economic fundamentals, like sterling and the Australian dollar, he added. "It's easier to trade, as you don't have to keep jumping at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shadows."  \par \par \uc2 Still, as most players believe the dollar's broad downtrend remains intact, it's likely only a matter of time before the euro resumes its uptrend, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y105.50, above Y105.48 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.39 late Friday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2727, lower than $1.2742 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.2813 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y134.26, down from Y134.40 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y135.03 in Tokyo late Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8820, down from $1.8860 in New York but little changed from $1.8919 in Tokyo Friday.  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040216e02g00063\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
