\par\par \b \uc2 JGBs little moved ahead of 20-yr offering.  \b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2004\par 04:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 16 (Reuters) - Japanese government bonds (JGB) barely budged from near recent multi-month peaks on Monday, with investors holding back ahead of a 20-year JGB auction set for Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Also obscuring the market's outlook were the yen, now hovering near a 3-= year high against the dollar, as market players are watching to see if the Japanese government's massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can stop its export-damaging rise.  \par \par \uc2 At midday, the key 10-year JGB futures contract for March delivery was down 0.02 point at 139.67. The contract hit a four-month high of 140 last Thursday as the yen's relentless rise stoked concerns about Japan's recovery.  \par \par \uc2 In the cash bond market, the benchmark 257th 10-year JGB yield was up one basis point at 1.250 percent, off a 4-1/2-month low of 1.220 percent hit last Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The current benchmark 65th 20-year JGBs were yielding 1.825 percent, up a half basis point.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to offer 500 billion yen ($4.74 billion) of 20-year JGBs through a price-competitive auction on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The coupon is seen likely to be set at 1.8 percent, compared with 1.9 percent in the previous four issues.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no reason to think the 20-year JGB auction will be heated," said Koji Ochiai, chief strategist at Nochu Securities.  \par \par \uc2 The market is also nervous as the tender will be followed by an offer of "super-long" 30-year JGBs next week.  \par \par \uc2 On the positive side, 20-year JGBs are now seen as relatively cheap.  \par \par \uc2 The spread between the 10-and 20-year yields is 57.5 basis points, near the widest level in six months.  \par \par \uc2 Still, analysts are quick to point out that the spread has stayed above 60 basis points for years in the past and it therefore hardly guarantees a good auction.  \par \par \uc2 Players were also keeping an eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as the yen's strength has been one of the major driving forces behind a rally in JGBs in the past few weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's appreciation is thought to be harmful for Japan's economic recovery - and good for safe-haven JGBs - as it cuts Japanese exporters' profits in yen terms and can make their goods less competitive overseas.  \par \par \uc2 The yen was trading around 105.42 yen per dollar on Monday, off last week's high near 105.15, which was its highest in nearly 3-= years, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year. ($1=105.45 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040216e02g00165\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
