\par\par \b \uc2 WRAP: Japan Voices Cautious Support For China  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Change  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 716 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 09:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Top Japanese officials said Friday they were encouraged by signs China may loosen its restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, a move that would allow the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise in value against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki and Economy Minister Heizo Takenaka said at regular news conferences that Tokyo was closely watching the debate over China's fixed-rate system.  \par \par \uc2 "I have expectations for a very big step forward," Takenaka said.  \par \par \uc2 The remarks come at a time of growing speculation that China might let its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , known alternatively as the yuan or the renminbi, move in a slightly wider band, bowing to calls from trading partners for it to do so.  \par \par \uc2 China keeps the yuan in a narrow band near CNY8.2770 to the dollar and restricts convertibility for trade-related purposes - controls that critics say keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly undervalued and give the world's most populous nation an unfair trade advantage.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao told a meeting of economic officials in Beijing that the government would maintain the "basic stability" of the yuan, but intends "to gradually perfect" its exchange-rate mechanism.  \par \par \uc2 China's State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  echoed that view in a statement Thursday, saying it would improve the yuan's exchange rate mechanism and keep the rate at a reasonable and balanced level.  \par \par \uc2 The statement prompted cautious approval from Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 "As a rule, the issue is up to China to decide, based on its own interests," Tanigaki said. "But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  systems must reflect underlying economies in a stable manner, or else they will become distorted.  \par \par \uc2 "We are watching this issue with interest," he added.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                  Yuan A Hot Topic After G7 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy has come under renewed scrutiny after a weekend meeting of the Group of Seven leading industrial nations, which resulted in a call for more flexibility among countries or economic areas that fall short in that regard.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That wording of that G7 statement has been interpreted as a criticism of fixed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regimes in China and other Asian nations.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan has long led the call for a revaluation of the yuan, arguing that an artificially weak exchange rate gives Chinese exporters an unfair edge over their Japanese competitors and exacerbates deflation in Japan through imports of cheap Chinese goods.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the cautious tone of Tanigaki and Takenaka's remarks illustrates Japan's delicate position over the yuan issue.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both officials talked about the yuan in response to questions from reporters rather than making their declarations without being prompted, and there's no sign now of Tokyo policy-makers launching a campaign to pressure China to change its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, Tokyo has kept to the sidelines during recent flare-ups over the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - most likely to avoid drawing attention to its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , afraid that an expensive yen could derail the nation's economic recovery by hurting exports, sold an unprecedented Y20.05 trillion in market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise last year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It has stepped up the pace of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, selling a record Y7.15 trillion in January alone.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With Japan taking a back seat on the yuan, the U.S. has stepped up pressure on China in Tokyo's stead, leading the G7's call for more flexibility  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some analysts have pointed to a planned visit by Chinese President Hu Jintao to the U.S. later this year as a possible time when China might relax its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime so that Hu will have a gift to take with him, in the form of policy that makes Washington happy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Toru Umemoto, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Morgan Stanley, said China is unlikely to radically overhaul its exchange control system soon.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "China's economy is strong but fragile, and Chinese authorities are going to delay a real revaluation as long as possible," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing may offer small concessions - such as a slightly wider trading band or looser capital controls. But a significant revaluation is at least a year away, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040213e02d000d0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
