\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Japan MOF Pressure Keeps Dollar Steady Vs Yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 06:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar held steady in a tight range against the yen in Asia Friday, as Japanese monetary authorities kept guard against any attempts to chase the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback also moved in a narrow band against the euro, as profit-taking continued to cap the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's topside after a recent surge close to its all-time high of $1.2899.  \par \par \uc2 Trading in Asia was generally subdued as market players took a breather after digesting events like last weekend's meeting of Group of Seven industrialized nations in Florida and Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's two-day semiannual congressional testimony that ended Thursday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 While these events did little to change the underlying dollar-bearish sentiment, market players were hesitant to test the greenback's downside as the specter of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  loomed large, they said.  \par \par \uc2 "As always, bids suspected to be from the ministry were supporting the dollar around Y105.00 to Y105.30," said a trader at a Japanese brokerage house.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo also made sure to keep up the pressure against dollar bears through verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Speaking before a Parliamentary budget committee, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki repeated the MOF's standard line that Tokyo was ready to take action if necessary to stem any sharp rise in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y105.39, above Y105.35 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.32 late Thursday in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2813, higher than $1.2804 late Thursday in New York but below $1.2829 in Tokyo Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.03, up from Y134.93 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y135.15 in Tokyo late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8919, up from $1.8915 in New York but lower than $1.8922 in Tokyo Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki admitted that the huge U.S. budget and trade deficits risk eroding the value of the dollar. But he was quick to warn that such financial imbalances won't be fixed through dollar weakness alone and that Washington is looking at ways to address the problem.  \par \par \uc2 "It's true that the twin deficits are a cause for concern," Tanigaki said. "But as Treasury Secretary Snow said repeatedly at the recent G7 meeting, the U.S. is addressing the issue."  \par \par \uc2 Senior Japanese bureaucrats also tried to keep the market on its toes by referring to joint \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  action with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the MOF's International Bureau, said Japan wouldn't rule out the possibility of carrying out coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the ECB to stem excessive exchange rate volatility.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pointman Zembei Mizoguchi then declined to comment on the issue Friday morning, leaving open the possibility of such action actually taking place.  \par \par \uc2 But Tohru Sasaki, strategist at J.P. Morgan Chase Bank's Tokyo branch, said the chances of such joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking place are extremely slim and that Watanabe was talking in a general way.  \par \par \uc2 "The ECB will act alone if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary" in its opinion, Sasaki said. "Besides, it doesn't seem to feel any imminent need to act now anyway."  \par \par \uc2 Traders, however, continued to test the ECB's patience on the rise of the euro. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crept as high as $1.2838 late in the afternoon session, and a Japanese bank trader warned the euro may charge ahead past $1.2900 once it breaks above key resistance at $1.2850.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson and Hugh Lawson  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040213e02d00063\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
