\par\par \b \uc2 Mizoguchi:No Comment On Possible ECB Joint  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 01:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A key Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official declined to comment Friday on whether the Japanese monetary authorities could conduct joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with their European counterparts.  \par \par \uc2 "We can't comment on such issues," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi said.  \par \par \uc2 A day earlier, another senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may consider carrying out coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed to stem excess exchange rate volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "We're not ruling out the possibility," said Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the ministry's International Bureau, when asked if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consider joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the dollar's slide.  \par \par \uc2 "Japan has said it will act, if needed, against excess volatility and disorderly movements. We will act in concert if needed," to curb disruptive moves, Watanabe said.  \par \par \uc2 But he added that it would be up to the ECB to decide to make any request for coordinated action.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040213e02d0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picsc