\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar hits 11-year low vs sterling, steady vs yen.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases   \par \uc2 706 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 08:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 13 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to an 11-year low against sterling as the well-worn "sell the greenback" theme re-emerged in late Asian trade on Friday but fears of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept it hemmed in a tight range against the yen.   \par \par \uc2 For much of the session the dollar moved little against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a heightened sensitivity to possible coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action having a lot to do with that, but sentiment towards the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained overwhelmingly bearish.   \par \par \uc2 "It seems that the dollar is being sold against higher yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Takashi Toyahara, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Securities in Tokyo, adding that "purchases of sterling was the key driver in the market right now", giving the euro its latest push up.   \par \par \uc2 Sterling reached $1.8971 its highest level since September 1992, before pulling back slightly to $1.8957, up 0.20 percent from late New York trade.   \par \par \uc2 The euro rose to $1.2821 up 0.15 percent on the day.   \par \par \uc2 "Unless U.S. or European officials warn against euro strength, there is a chance that the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could test record highs," Toyahara added.   \par \par \uc2 The euro hit an all-time high just under $1.29 on January 12.   \par \par \uc2 Investors continued to dump the dollar in search of assets in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  bringing higher yields, such as the Australian dollar. The benchmark interest rate in Australia is 5.25 percent versus 1.0 percent in the United States.   \par \par \uc2 Earlier, the Australian dollar hit a seven-year high against the U.S. dollar at around US$0.7921   \par \par \uc2 With Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan saying this week he was not overly concerned with the dollar's decline and its potential to spark inflation, interest rates in the United States are not expected to change for the time being.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar moved in a tight range against the yen, hovering near 105.40 yen according to Reuters data.   \par \par \uc2 "Heavy options-related selling is expected under 105 yen and I think the authorities know this so they aren't going to let it break that level so easily," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group at UFJ Bank.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was not aimed at keeping the yen at a particular level, but that it would take decisive steps against excessive moves.   \par \par \uc2 Investors remain wary of the willingness and ability of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar. In January alone, they spent a record seven trillion yen ($66.45 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "There must be some very keen defence of dollar/yen around 105.30," said Jake Moore, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Bank in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 EXPANDED \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?   \par \par \uc2 Earlier, Zembei Mizoguchi, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, would not comment when asked by reporters if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with European authorities to stop their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising in value against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international division, said on Thursday that the government could not rule out coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "At the moment there is no coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it seems unlikely that there will be. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would love it, it would be very favourable for their policy. That said, people are getting nervous that the ECB could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the months ahead. I personally don't think they will," said Barclays' Moore.   \par \par \uc2 UFJ's Sahara said: "There is some caution about pushing the euro to record highs after G7 (Group of Seven) countries warned against excessive volatility, although I don't think European officials will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 Ahead of the long President's Day holiday weekend in the United States, investors will get a healthy portion of U.S. economic data. At 1330 GMT, international trade data are expected to show the deficit increased to $40 billion in December from $38.01 billion in November.   \par \par \uc2 The February preliminary University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey is due at around 1445 GMT, with economists forecasting a small decline to 103.3 from 103.8 in January. (Additional reporting by Kazunori Takada in Tokyo) ($1=105.34 yen).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040213e02d00198\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
