\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar drifts as market casts wary eye on BOJ.    \b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Bases    \par \uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 07:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 13 (Reuters) - The dollar was nearly unchanged against its major counterparts on Friday, hemmed in versus the yen by fear of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a heightened sensitivity to possible coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action.    \par \par \uc2 In mid-afternoon Tokyo trade, the Australian dollar extended slightly to a fresh seven-year high against the U.S. dollar around US$0.7913 .    \par \par \uc2 While market trade was relatively quiet, the underlying theme of dollar selling remained firmly entrenched.    \par \par \uc2 Investors continue to dump the dollar in search of assets with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  bringing higher yields, such as Australia where the benchmark interest rate is 5.25 percent versus 1.0 percent in the United States.    \par \par \uc2 With Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan saying this week he is not overly concerned with the dollar's decline and its potential to spark inflation, interest rates in the United States are not expected to change for the time being.    \par \par \uc2 The euro was also little changed from late New York trade at $1.2805 .    \par \par \uc2 The dollar moved in a tight trading range against the yen, hovering near 105.38 yen according to Reuters data.    \par \par \uc2 "Heavy options-related selling is expected under 105 yen and I think the authorities know this so they aren't going to let it break that level so easily," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group at UFJ Bank.    \par \par \uc2 Investors remain wary of the willingness and ability of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the dollar. In January alone, they spent a record seven trillion yen ($66.45 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2 "There must be some very keen defence of dollar/yen around 105.30," said Jake Moore, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Bank in Tokyo.    \par \par \uc2 EXPANDED \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?    \par \par \uc2 Earlier, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, would not comment when asked by reporters if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with European authorities to stop their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising in value against the dollar.    \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi's decision not to comment comes one day after Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international division, said on Thursday the government could not rule out the possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2 "At the moment there is no coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it seems unlikely that there will be. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would love it, it would be very favourable for their policy. That said, people are getting nervous that the ECB could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the months ahead. I personally don't think they will," said Barclays' Moore.    \par \par \uc2 The euro hit an all-time high just under $1.29 on January 12.    \par \par \uc2 "There is some caution about pushing the euro to record highs after G7 (Group of Seven) countries warned against excess volatility, although I don't think European officials will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said UFJ's Sahara.    \par \par \uc2 U.S. DATA    \par \par \uc2 Ahead of the long President's Day holiday weekend in the United States, investors will get a healthy portion of U.S. economic data. At 1330 GMT, international trade data is expected to show the deficit increased to $40 billion in December from $38.01 billion in November.    \par \par \uc2 Additionally, the February preliminary University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey is due at around 1445 GMT, with economists forecasting a small decline to 103.3 from 103.8 in January. (Additional reporting by Kazunori Takada in Tokyo) ($1=105.34 yen).     \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040213e02d000pb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
