\par\par \b \uc2 Japan spends stopgap funds but can still act on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 04:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 13 (Reuters) - Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets has resulted in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government using up funds from a stopgap scheme to sell foreign bonds to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to finance it, Bank of Japan (BOJ) data showed on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  But the government is still able to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in which it seeks to curb the yen's rise against the dollar, as it has boosted funding for it through more conventional means.   \par \par \uc2  BOJ accounts data showed its "receivables under resales agreements" jumped to 15.06 trillion yen ($143 billion) as of February 10 from 10.20 trillion yen on January 31.   \par \par \uc2  Stripping out the BOJ's other transactions under resale agreements, such as some open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ's buying of foreign bonds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the period was seen at around five trillion yen.   \par \par \uc2  That, in addition to five trillion yen the BOJ was seen buying earlier in January, meant the government probably used up the whole of 10 trillion yen from a framework set up last year to temporarily sell foreign bonds, part of its official reserves, to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Normally the ministry pays for its dollar buying in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by raising yen funds through financing bills.   \par \par \uc2  But due to aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last year the ministry is suspected of having exhausted its funds, forcing it to seek stopgap measures.   \par \par \uc2  Parliament last week agreed to raise the limit of debt the government can issue to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 100 trillion yen from 79 trillion yen for the year ending in March.   \par \par \uc2  The government is also seeking to raise the borrowing limit to 140 trillion yen in the fiscal year starting in April.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a record 20 trillion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year and sold another seven trillion in January, but the yen has continued to rise. It hit a three-year high of 105.16 yen  on Wednesday. Early on Friday afternoon in Tokyo it was around 105.42 yen. ($1=105.34 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040213e02d000k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
