\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Slips To New 1-Month Low Against Euro  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 811 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2004\par 06:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar remained under pressure against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia Thursday, hitting a fresh one-month low against the euro and avoiding a new three-and-a-half-year low against the yen only with the apparent support of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.  \par \par \uc2 The euro edged above its Wednesday peak of $1.2838 to $1.2844, its highest level since Jan. 12, when European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet sent it tumbling with his warning against "brutal" exchange rate moves.  \par \par \uc2 "It's only a matter of time" before the euro tests the all-time high of $1.2899 set before Trichet's verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Satoshi Tate, a vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at UFJ Bank.  \par \par \uc2 More verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from European officials and profit taking by euro bulls are likely to slow the single unit's rise around $1.30, he said, but added that any setback would likely be temporary.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's latest blow came from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, who said on the first of two days of Congressional testimony Wednesday that the greenback's "gradual" depreciation hasn't hurt U.S. capital markets and "should eventually help to contain our current account deficit."  \par \par \uc2 Traders were looking to day two of Greenspan's testimony for further clues about the Fed's stance on the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 In Tokyo, meanwhile, a top \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen moves sharply higher.  \par \par \uc2 "We will take action as needed," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi said, adding the MOF's standard line that excessive exchange rate moves are undesirable.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities placed covert bids to support the dollar around Y105.30. But there was no sign of an aggressive effort to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher.  \par \par \uc2 "Right now defensive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is all they can do," said UFJ's Tate. "With the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also being bought against the dollar, they have no excuse to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively."  \par \par \uc2 Tate predicted the dollar would fall to Y104.00 by the end of January.  \par \par \uc2 Around 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y105.32, just below Y105.35 late Wednesday in New York. The dollar was at Y105.44 late Wednesday in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo markets were closed Wednesday due to a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2829, a shade higher than $1.2826 late Wednesday in New York. The euro was at $1.2703 in Singapore Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y135.15, slightly above Y135.12 in New York late Wednesday. The euro was at Y133.95 in Singapore late Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.8922, up from $1.8912 in New York and higher than $1.8700 in Singapore Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 While most traders expect the dollar to decline gradually against the yen in the weeks and months ahead, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has convinced at least a few dollar bears to look for profits elsewhere.  \par \par \uc2 "It's a waste of your position allotment" to chase moves in the dollar/yen, a Tokyo bank dealer said. "People are looking at the euro, at high-yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at yen-crosses."  \par \par \uc2 That could slow the pace of the dollar's decline against the yen even further, he said.  \par \par \uc2 In addition, options-related barriers around Y105 are likely to bolster MOF's defense of that level, he said.  \par \par \uc2 With MOF said to be in the market, even strong Japanese economic data failed to knock the dollar/yen out of its narrow range.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's current account surplus grew 38.5% from a year earlier in December, the government said, marking the sixth straight month of expansion despite the yen's 12% appreciation versus the dollar during the year.  \par \par \uc2 Also in December, Japanese core machinery orders rebounded 8.1% from the previous month, a much larger gain than the 1.9% rise forecast on average by economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 December's jump followed a 7.8% tumble in November and helped lift the leading indicator for fixed business outlays by 11.3% in the October-December quarter.  \par \par \uc2 The firm fourth-quarter showing underscores the government's view that business expenditures are increasing and remain on a recovery track on continued improvements in corporate earnings.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates that accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribers can find this table:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040212e02c00058\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
