\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar up from 1-mo lows vs euro, awaits Greenspan.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Burton Frierson  \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2004\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 11 (Reuters) - The dollar held steady against the euro on Wednesday above the previous session's one-month low before testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan that markets will scrutinise for hints of interest rate hikes.  \par \par \uc2 Yield-boosting rate rises are key to ending the dollar's decline, especially after the Group of Seven nations made no promises at a weekend meeting to support it in the event of the "disorderly movements in exchange rates" that concern them.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed sparked speculation of an earlier-than-expected rate hike when it changed its emphasis in its last policy statement. Weak U.S. jobs data subsequently gave markets pause for thought although other figures suggest the recovery is holding up.  \par \par \uc2 "The risk is that Greenspan is slightly more hawkish," said Ian Stannard, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 "That could cause some extra volatility, initially providing support for the dollar, but after that we have to look at how the bond market reacts to assess the medium-term effects on euro/dollar."  \par \par \uc2 By 1100 GMT, the dollar trimmed its earlier gains to trade steady on the day at $1.2685, up from Tuesday's one-month low at $1.2788.  \par \par \uc2 It was steady at 105.52 yen but remained close to last week's three-year lows around 105.20. Expectations of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit yen rises, balanced by exporters' dollar offers have recently kept the yen relatively stable against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Against sterling, the greenback was steady on the day at $1.8712 just above the previous session's 11-year low of $1.8734.  \par \par \uc2 In its quarterly Inflation Report, the Bank of England said it expected inflation to pick up sharply this year, boosting the pound briefly against the dollar and the euro as the hawkish tone kept British rate hike expectations firm.  \par \par \uc2 FED WATCHING  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan delivers his semi-annual monetary policy testimony to the House of Representatives' Financial Services Committee at 1600 GMT, and to the Senate Banking Committee on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts expect Greenspan to tell Congress that U.S. economic prospects are good but to stress the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be patient before upping interest rates from 1958 lows.  \par \par \uc2 They also expect Greenspan to assure lawmakers that inflation is unlikely to flare up soon, given a weak job market and lots of spare productive capacity.  \par \par \uc2 While analysts noted that dollar weakness was a function of foreign investors' unwillingness to fund the U.S. current account deficit, the dollar could still get a short-term boost if Greenspan gave a robust outlook for the economy.  \par \par \uc2 "Although we are still in a structurally bearish trend, and the G7 outcome obviously reinforced that, we are perhaps looking at a pause in the long dollar decline as Greenspan delivers a relatively upbeat testimony," said Adam Cole, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez in London.  \par \par \uc2 "Equally there is probably a risk that he talks about some return of pricing power to the corporate sector in the U.S. - i.e. further diminishing deflation fears. Again, that should be relatively dollar supportive."  \par \par \uc2 U.S. lawmakers are also likely to take the opportunity to grill the Fed chief on U.S. fiscal policy.  \par \par \uc2 The Bush administration has forecast a record $521 billion deficit this year - adding to the dollar's woes - but has vowed to cut that in half by 2009.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040211e02b002x8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
