\par\par \b \uc2 WRAP: MOF Tanigaki Says Japan Happy With G7  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Words  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Miyako Takebe and Jonathan Soble  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 767 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2004\par 08:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister said Tuesday Tokyo got the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement it wanted at the weekend G7 meeting, and cautioned that recent moves in major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been at odds with economic realities.  \par \par \uc2 Considering how strong the U.S. economy is compared with its European and Japanese counterparts, the market ought to be in love with the dollar rather than the euro and yen, said Minister of Finance Sadakazu Tanigaki.  \par \par \uc2 "I just hope that if the (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market is a beauty contest, players will choose the real beauty and not the one that they think everyone will think is beautiful," he said, alluding to a metaphor thought up by the economist John Maynard Keynes.  \par \par \uc2 The finance minister also suggested in parliamentary testimony that China ought to consider relaxing its tight grip on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though adding that's a decision for Beijing should make itself.  \par \par \uc2 His remarks follow a meeting last week of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the Group of Seven rich countries in Boca Raton, Fla., where the group cautioned against excessively volatile and disorderly moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - a declaration that markets interpreted as pointing to the dollar's tumble against the yen and euro.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki said the G7's statement, which also called for more \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate flexibility in major economic areas that have inflexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes, "turned out in a way in which everyone was happy."  \par \par \uc2 Japanese and European policy-makers might not be very happy, though, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves this week after the G7. The dollar remains near a three-and-a-half year low against the yen, at a time when Tokyo wants the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be weak to support exports.  \par \par \uc2 At 0641 GMT, the dollar was trading near the day's low at Y105.42, and the euro near the day's high of $1.2743.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki declined to comment Tuesday on how exchange rates have moved since the meeting of the G7, which consists of the U.S., Japan, Germany, France, the U.K., Italy and Canada.  \par \par \uc2 Many market players expect the dollar to continue weakening for now, though, as the widening U.S. current account and budget deficits chill sentiment toward the greenback.  \par \par \uc2 "The G7 event is over," said Masamichi Koike, head of spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp. "What's clear now is that there's been no correction to the weak-dollar trend."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par             Japan Says It's Flexible On \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Tanigaki also touched on another section of the G7's statement that urged more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flexibility in big economic areas that fall short in that regard.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He repeated that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , despite heavy-handed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past year, isn't one of those countries with a rigid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is the common understanding of the G7 that Japan is not a country which lacks flexibility," Tanigaki said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He appeared to consider China, which keeps its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan, in a tight range against the dollar, one of those countries that ought to make its exchange rate freer to move.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There are two basic principles on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which are accepted internationally. The first is that each country should set its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy based on its own national interests," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The second principle is that it's desirable to have a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime in which rates reflect fundamentals in a stable manner."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China keeps the yuan pegged to a wafer-thin trading range against the dollar, a system that many economists say keeps the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sharply undervalued against the dollar given China's explosive economic growth in recent years.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan is expected to strengthen if Beijing relaxes its control of the exchange rate, but the Chinese government hasn't shown any signs it is ready to do so.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, a spokesman for China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday: "Currently the bank has no specific plans for renminbi changes. There is no timetable for renminbi reform." The yuan is also known as renminbi, or people's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan, for its part, signaled it will continue with its aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaign, in which it sold record Y20 trillion last year and a staggering Y7 trillion in January alone.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There is no change from our previous stance" on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Zembei Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, said Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Miyako Takebe & Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com, jonathan.soble@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040210e02a000av\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
