\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  No Change In Japan  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Policy Post-G7  \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2004\par 07:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's monetary authorities appeared keen to avoid a recurrence of the Dubai G7 experience, when the communique's call for "flexibility" in exchange rates was widely interpreted as criticism of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and caused the yen to surge against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Boca Raton statement retained the call for flexibility and added a portion saying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility was desirable "for major countries or economic areas that lack such flexibility" in order to promote smooth adjustments in the international finance system.  \par \par \uc2 Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international bureau, chose to highlight the phrase warning against "excess volatility," saying it applied not only to euro/dollar rates but also to dollar/yen movements.  \par \par \uc2 "The phrase means if there is excess volatility or inappropriate moves in the market, we will take necessary action," Watanabe said, suggesting the MOF's determination to keep acting to prevent the yen's sharp rise from hurting Japan's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 Tomoko Fujii, strategist at Nikko Citigroup, expects \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance to remain largely unchanged from that before the G7 meeting.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only up to a level where it won't be interpreted as intentionally guiding the yen lower, so that the United States can tolerate it," Fujii said.  \par \par \uc2 Fujii believes the MOF will try to keep defending the Y105 line, where many Japanese export firms have set their in-house exchange rate forecasts.  \par \par \uc2 But the dollar/yen's line-in-the-sand may be shifted lower, or toward further yen strength, "if Japan's economic indicators, exporters' earnings and stock prices show firmness" and lead to a higher yen, she said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alastair Gale  \par \par \uc2 The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly.  \par \par \uc2 Subscribers can find this table:  \par \par \uc2 -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.  \par \par \uc2 -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX  \par \par \uc2 -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT  \par \par \uc2 -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040209e0290007l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
